<?xml version='1.0' standalone='yes'?>
<!DOCTYPE PLUGIN>

<PLUGIN 
  name="app-update-helper"
  author="Mark Haakman"
  version="0.3.0"
  launch="Settings/AUH-Settings"
  pluginURL="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/MarkHaakman/unraid-apps-update-helper/main/plugin/app-update-helper.plg"
  
  min="7.0.0"
  
  icon="arrow-circle-o-up"
>

<CHANGES>
<![CDATA[

### 0.3.0

## ✨ New: restore a container from a backup

- A **Restore** action on the Docker tab lists the container's backups and brings one back.
- The current appdata is moved aside (kept with a `.pre-restore` suffix), the archive is extracted in place, and the container is recreated from its template with the image it ran when the backup was made, pulled again by its registry digest.
- If anything fails, the previous appdata, image tag and container are put back. A backup whose image differs from the one the container uses now is refused.
- Rolling back a restore only ever deletes plain appdata folders at least three levels below `/mnt` (`/mnt/<pool>/<share>/<folder>`), so a disk, pool or share is never removed; volumes outside that rule are refused before anything is moved.

## 🔧 Changes

- Backup archive names now include the application version. Retention sorts backups by modification time.
- Backups record the image and digest in a JSON sidecar, and archives store full paths (`mnt/user/appdata/<name>/`) so each folder is restored exactly where it came from.
- The backup destination on the settings page uses Unraid's folder picker.

## Notes

- Only backups made with 0.3.0 or later can be restored, as older archives don't store full paths. A backup without an image sidecar restores appdata only.
- Listing and restoring backups requires a valid backup destination.

**Full Changelog**: https://github.com/MarkHaakman/unraid-apps-update-helper/compare/0.2.0...0.3.0

### 0.2.0

## ✨ New: update containers from the Docker tab

- **Update** and **Backup & Update** buttons on every row with an available update (containers created from an Unraid Docker template).
- A job status badge per container and a live log viewer while an update runs.
- Jobs are queued and processed one at a time by a background worker, so several updates can be started in a row.
- **Backup & Update** stops the container, archives its appdata bind mounts, updates it through Unraid's own `update_container`, and restarts it if it was running.
- If a backup or update fails, the update is skipped, the container's running state is restored and an Unraid notification is raised.

## ⚙️ New: settings page

**Settings > User Utilities > App Update Helper** configures the backup destination, appdata roots, exclusions, compression, whether to stop the container during the backup, and how many backups to keep.

## 🔧 Changes

- Containers are now started and stopped through Unraid's `DockerClient`, the same code path as the Docker tab (honours Unraid's stop timeout and WireGuard routes), instead of the `docker` CLI.
- Refreshed plugin descriptions (README, Community Applications listing, package description).

## Notes

- Backups stop the container using Unraid's configured Docker stop timeout.
- The plugin only updates containers that have an Unraid template (`my-<name>.xml`); others are shown but have no update buttons.

**Full Changelog**: https://github.com/MarkHaakman/unraid-apps-update-helper/compare/0.1.0...0.2.0

### 0.1.0

**Full Changelog**: https://github.com/MarkHaakman/unraid-apps-update-helper/commits/0.1.0


For older releases, see https://github.com/MarkHaakman/unraid-apps-update-helper/releases
]]>
</CHANGES>

<FILE Name="/boot/config/plugins/app-update-helper/unraid-apps-update-helper-0.3.0-noarch-1.txz">
<URL>https://github.com/MarkHaakman/unraid-apps-update-helper/releases/download/0.3.0/unraid-apps-update-helper-0.3.0-noarch-1.txz</URL>
<SHA256>0c95d31c0a781d67c14d8955eb228c602abd4492e59ad924630f99714bc80e17</SHA256>
</FILE>

<!--
The 'install' script.
-->
<FILE Run="/bin/bash">
<INLINE>
<![CDATA[
upgradepkg --install-new /boot/config/plugins/app-update-helper/unraid-apps-update-helper-0.3.0-noarch-1.txz

# cleanup old versions
rm -f $(ls /boot/config/plugins/app-update-helper/unraid-apps-update-helper-*.txz 2>/dev/null | grep -v '0.3.0')

echo ""
echo "----------------------------------------------------"
echo " app-update-helper has been installed."
echo " Version: 0.3.0"
echo "----------------------------------------------------"
echo ""
]]>
</INLINE>
</FILE>

<!--
The 'remove' script.
-->
<FILE Run="/bin/bash" Method="remove">
<INLINE>
<![CDATA[
removepkg unraid-apps-update-helper

rm -rf /usr/local/emhttp/plugins/app-update-helper
rm -rf /boot/config/plugins/app-update-helper
rm -rf /tmp/app-update-helper
]]>
</INLINE>
</FILE>

</PLUGIN>
